From 3c68066883107fe85fa96e12eaf4c736383d2d64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yankneck696 <yankneck696@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:33:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/14] PlutoSDR: read up to four waiting receive blocks per
 tick through a full-duplex over (#525)

During a full-duplex over the engine reads one 16384-sample block per
10 ms tick, a 1.64 Msps ceiling: a 2.083 Msps PlutoSDR fell further behind
with every tick and dropped a fifth of its receive at its own ring, which is
also PureSignal's feedback.

IqSource gains full_duplex_reads_per_tick(), default 1, which the
transverter wrapper forwards. The Pluto answers 4: up to four blocks a tick
when that many are already waiting, still never waiting for more, each going
to the panadapter as well as the audio, as #652 made it. Every other
full-duplex source (LimeSDR, SoapySX, HackRF and the rest) keeps the one
block a tick it has been tested with, since on SoapySX a transmit block that
goes out late is heard as chirps.
