Subject: [PATCH 12/14] PlutoSDR PureSignal: start RX2 at 0 dB, say at open why
 the PTT pins rule it out, and update the manual (#525)

From the review of #743.

- Choosing PureSignal for RX2 in the settings now brings RX2's gain down to
  0 dB if it was higher. The default the block shares with the LimeSDR's
  second chain, 40 dB, suits a second aerial; on a coupler it overloads RX2
  with a typical tap. On a PlutoSky R2 with a 46 dB tap, 0 dB was right and
  10-20 dB already drove RX2 into compression (the envelope match fell to
  0.7-0.8 and the table scattered). Only the switch to PureSignal does this:
  a gain set afterwards is left alone.
- With the PTT pins on, PureSignal was already refused at open, since they
  put the AD9361 in TDD and so take full duplex away, but the note blamed
  full duplex. It now names the pins, says why they rule it out, and what to
  set instead. The note is on screen through the open status, so it is not
  left to an over that never locks.
- The manual says the same, and that PureSignal has now been verified on a
  PlutoSky R2, where it said it had not.
